## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Sonnet 4.6
- **Short description:** Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.6 is a legacy Sonnet model with adaptive thinking and 1M-token context (GA-era positioning), now succeeded by Claude Sonnet 5.5.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic Claude API `claude-sonnet-4-6`; available on multiple Anthropic-supported platforms per platform docs. Local metadata lists `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6` and `noFreeId` (with trial quota notes).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released February 17, 2026. Reliable knowledge cutoff August 2025; training data cutoff January 2026 (Anthropic platform docs).
- **IDs:** `claude-sonnet-4-6`, `anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` (platform-specific).
- **Context window:** 1M tokens context, 128K max output (synchronous Messages API; 300K batch beta supported per docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (Anthropic platform docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $3 / 1M input tokens, $15 / 1M output tokens; cache read $0.30 / 1M, 5m cache write $3.75 / 1M, 1h cache write $6 / 1M, Batch API 50% discount (Anthropic platform docs).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Anthropic model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

